# `lines(source: Trimmed)`: a trimmed source may be a feed, `Feed(Trimmed, Cached)`, so `Trimmed.read`'s
# `super().read()` runs `Source.read`, or on a feed the next `read` after `Trimmed` along the feed's order: `Cached.read`
# on the feed (#155). There it reads the store before it asks the network, and its own `super().read()` runs
# `Source.read` on the feed, which is no recursion: the alternative runs in place of the `Source.read` its call reaches.
# Every `read` gives bytes, no type of the code's: it goes back to the call that ran it. The store is read in one arm
# and written in the other; arms of one choice never run one after the other, so the route finds what is there and
# changes it. What a call runs on through `self` is the source the route is handed.

route news.read.lines
step lines/Trimmed.read
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read                                                    # `super().read()`, a choice
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen                                            # `with urlopen(self.url) as response`
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read                                        # what it runs on a feed
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/Store.has
choice lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.get
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read                         # `super().read()` on the feed
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.put

line entry > lines call
line Trimmed·source > lines value
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen value         # `urlopen(self.url)`
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen > _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen value
line _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read value   # `response.read()`
line Web > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read own                                         # `urlopen(self.url)` with no data is a GET
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read > lines/Trimmed.read back
line lines/Trimmed.read > lines back
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/Store.has value   # `self.store.has(self.url)`
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/Store.has > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read back
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.get value
line Disk(self.root / key) > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.get own
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.get > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read back
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen value
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen > _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen value
line _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read value
line Web > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read own
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > _·data@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read value
line _·data@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.put value
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.put value
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.put > Disk(self.root / key) own
line _·data@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read value   # `return data`
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read back

# the values a call is handed through `self` drawn as types from beyond, and the source at the own arrow

home Trimmed·source lines
home _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read
home _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read
home _·data@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/Cached.read   # `return data` uses it too

side entry left
side Web left                                                                         # `urlopen(url)` with no data is a GET
side Disk(self.root / key) both

# `cached_lines(source: Cached)`: a cached source may be a feed, `Feed(Trimmed, Cached)`, which runs `Trimmed.read` for
# `read`, so the call is `Cached.read` or, on a feed, `Trimmed.read` on the feed (#155), drawn as the feed's method,
# `Feed.read`. Its `super().read()` runs the next `read` after `Trimmed` along the feed's order: `Cached.read` on the
# feed, which reads the store before it asks the network. Either way the source is read through its store: what
# `cached_lines` runs on a feed does what it does on any cached source, as a cache that is also trimmed should.

route news.read.cached_lines
step cached_lines/Cached.read                                                     # `source.read()`, one of two
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Store.has
choice cached_lines/Cached.read/?1
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.get
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read                                      # `super().read()`
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.put
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read                                           # what it runs on a feed
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read                               # `super().read()` on the feed
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/Store.has
choice cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/?1
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.get
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read                # Cached's `super().read()` on the feed
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Cached.read/?1/Store.put

